   271	The automorphism A is the following {n} by {n} matrix (one row per line):
   272	BEGIN_MATRIX
   273	{rows}
   274	END_MATRIX
   275	
   276	Find B, but return it in the required normalized factored form
   277	  B = I + alpha * left * right^T.
   278	Here alpha is a nonzero residue; left and right are length-{n} vectors whose
   279	entries are all nonzero residues; left[0] must equal 1; and right[0] must equal
   280	A[0][0]-1 modulo {p}.  This normalization makes the representation unique.
   281	The checker expands the factorization and verifies B*A^T=I exactly.  Vector
   282	order matters, indices are 0-based, no position may be omitted, and residue
   283	values may repeat.
   284	
   285	Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags as one JSON object with
   286	exactly the keys alpha, left, and right, with integer residues as values.
   287	Example: <answer>{{"alpha":1,"left":[1{',1' * (n - 1)}],"right":[{(inst['automorphism'][0][0] - 1) % p}{',1' * (n - 1)}]}}</answer>
   288	Output nothing else inside the tags."""
   289	    mode = os.environ.get("GV_HINT_MODE")
   290	    if mode == "structural":
   291	        statement += "\n\nHint: " + STRUCTURAL_HINT
   292	    elif mode == "placebo":
   293	        statement += "\n\nHint: " + PLACEBO_HINT
   294	    return statement
