  1228	\item[(4)] $\la_t>0$ for $1 \le t \le 3$ and $\{SS^{(-1)}\} \cap (H_i \sm (H_j \cup H_l)) \ne \es$.
  1229	\end{itemize}
  1230	\end{lemma}
  1231	\begin{proof}
  1232	Since $S$ has rank three and $H_1,H_2,H_3$ are three maximal subgroups, then for any $x,y \in S$, we have $xy^{-1} \in H_1 \cup H_2 \cup H_3$. Recall that by Lemma~\ref{lem-prieven}(2), $H_1 \cap H_2 \cap H_3=\{1\}$. Without loss of generality, we assume $1 \in S$.
  1233	
  1234	(1) Suppose otherwise, that $x \in S_i$ and $y \in S_{jl}$. Then $xy^{-1} \notin H_1 \cup H_2 \cup H_3$, which contradicts the property of even sets.
