  1245	For primitive formally dual sets of rank three, we have the following characterization.
  1246	
  1247	\begin{theorem}\label{thm-rankthree}
  1248	If $S$ is a primitive formally dual set of rank three in $G$, then $S$ is an $(n,n,n,1)$-RDS in $G$ with $n>1$.
