codex
Implemented the Track B generator based on Propositions 2.13, 2.16, and 3.2 of the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1804.06328).

Deliverables:

- [gen_1804_06328.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1804.06328/gen_1804_06328.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1804.06328/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1804.06328/README.md)
- [bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1804.06328/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1804.06328/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1804.06328/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All local gates pass:

- G1: 16/16 planted certificates verified.
- G4: 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses.
- G6: four attacks failed 0/8; the Track B reference algorithm succeeds 8/8.
- G8: 20/20 invariance and carried-witness tests.
- G9(c): 750 characters, 181 atoms, 272 operations.

The result is not yet submission-ready: the hard oracle level recorded two genuine failures, but OpenRouter exhausted its total key quota before the required third attempt. The hinted and placebo arms likewise contain quota errors rather than scored attempts. This is recorded honestly as `oracle_evidence_complete: false`; no hardness verdict was fabricated.
