{"schema_version": 2, "model": "google/gemini-3.8-flash", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 90, "p": 997}, "seed": 1220172002, "solved": "failed", "parsed": false, "verify_ok": null, "verify_reason": "parse_answer returned None", "reply": "To find the normalized factored form $B = I + \\alpha \\cdot \\text{left} \\cdot \\text{right}^T = (A^T)^{-1}$, we analyze the structure of the given $90 \\times 90$ automorphism matrix $A$ over $\\mathbb{F}_{997}$.\n\n### 1. Structure of $A$\nInspecting the matrix $A$, we find that $A - I$ is a rank-1 matrix:\n$$A - I = c r^T$$\nwhere $c$ is a column vector and $r^T$ is a row vector. For every off-diagonal element, $A[i][j] = c_i r_j$, and on the diagonal, $A[i][i] = c_i r_i + 1$. \n\nBy the Sherman\u2013Morrison formula:\n$$(A^T)^{-1} = (I + r c^T)^{-1} = I - \\frac{1}{1 + c^T r} r c^T$$\nComparing this with $B = I + \\alpha \\cdot \\text{left} \\cdot \\text{right}^T$:\n- Under the required normalizations $\\text{left}[0] = 1$ and $\\text{right}[0] = A[0][0] - 1 = 636$:\n  $$\\text{right}[j] = (A - I)_{j, 0} = \\begin{cases} A[0][0] - 1 = 636 & \\text{if } j = 0 \\\\ A[j][0] & \\text{if } j \\ge 1 \\end{cases}$$\n  $$\\text{left}[i] = (A - I)_{0, i} \\cdot 636^{-1} \\pmod{997}$$\n\n### 2. Computing $\\alpha$ and the Vectors\nThe inverse of $636$ modulo $997$ is:\n$$636^{-1} \\equiv 939 \\equiv -58 \\pmod{997}$$\n\nThe linear transformation $A$ is an involution ($A^2 = I$), which corresponds to an elementary reflection across a hyperplane. For an involution with $A - I = c r^T$, the trace is $c^T r = -2 \\pmod{997}$, yielding:\n$$\\alpha = -\\frac{1}{1 + c^T r} = -\\frac{1}{1 - 2} = 1$$\n\nThus, $\\alpha = 1$, and:\n- $\\text{right}$ is the 0-th column of $A - I$:\n  $$\\text{right} = [636, A[1][0], A[2][0], \\dots, A[89][0]]$$\n- $\\text{left}$ is the 0-th row of $A - I$ multiplied by $939 \\pmod{997}$:\n  $$\\text{left}[0] = 1, \\quad \\text{left}[i] = (A[0][i] \\times 939) \\pmod{997} \\quad (1 \\le i \\le 89)$$\n\nComputing $\\text{left}[i] = A[0][i] \\times (-58) \\pmod{997}$ for each entry of Row 0:\n- $i=0: 1$\n- $i=1: 527 \\times (-58) \\equiv 341$\n- $i=2: 925 \\times (-58) \\equiv 196$\n- $i=3: 800 \\times (-58) \\equiv 475$\n- and likewise for all remaining coordinates.\n\n<answer>{\"alpha\":1,\"left\":[1,341,196,475,324,107,208,879,72,612,854,82,41,727,411,749,343,580,865,221,387,42,42,829,598,995,431,987,947,4,228,642,844,929,835,216,664,216,930,713,717,737,867,864,834,706,290,729,505,475,394,40,29,209,47,432,797,185,671,325,72,168,324,149,717,67,138,984,402,408,854,142,260,61,977,20,795,553,52,693,585,400,111,623,680,24,699,417,921,848],\"right\":[636,102,760,455,420,162,860,862,748,761,54,139,378,977,213,909,544,188,561,690,589,355,", "error": null, "elapsed_sec": 191.71, "http_status": 200, "finish_reason": "length", "preset": "hard", "escalation_round": 2}
